Third-party skill documents: methodology references
=================================================

The following reference documents are DSH adaptations of material from
brooks-lint, a code-review skill set grounded in twelve classic software
engineering books:

  hyhmrright, "brooks-lint"
  https://github.com/hyhmrright/brooks-lint
  commit 5beb35b040e3de97e54fa9e386d7e42d15c295c2 (vendored via
  /home/dev/dsh-brooks-lint-dsh 0.1.0)

Adapted files:

  - assets/skills/independent-code-review-workflow/references/decay-risks.md
  - assets/skills/independent-code-review-workflow/references/test-quality-review.md
  - assets/skills/backend-architecture-workflow/references/architecture-audit.md
  - assets/skills/backend-architecture-workflow/references/architecture-decay-risks.md
  - assets/skills/fullstack-advisor/references/brooks-principles.md

These files are Chinese rewrites, not copies. They keep the upstream
risk taxonomy (R1-R6 and T1-T6), the four-part finding structure, and the
"what not to flag" guards; they drop the upstream runtime protocol
(.brooks-lint.yaml configuration, health scoring, history tracking, --fix
and full-sweep auto-remediation, and slash-command integration), which has
no counterpart in this plugin. The book attributions the upstream material
carries are kept as method provenance.

